# The controller's build context: controller/ and api/, and nothing else.
#
# BuildKit uses this file in preference to the repository's .dockerignore
# because it sits beside the Dockerfile it belongs to. The point is not build
# speed: it is that the component holding a customer's git tokens cannot
# accidentally acquire the fakes, the test harness or the agent image, and that
# this stops depending on nobody writing the wrong COPY.
*
!api/
!controller/

# Not even from the two directories that are in.
**/.git
**/node_modules
**/.DS_Store
controller/Dockerfile*
